{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1789 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "65755ce7c9644c27dd5520f498ed469fecd1e3a83057c9c700686f133699cd94" :edb/db-before-t 1788 :edb/db-after-t 1789 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535101 50 #inst "2026-10-08T16:50:25.214Z" 13194139535101 true] [17592186091972 1100 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2x+5y-2z=-2 \\\\ -3y+z=-2 \\\\ 3x-7y+3z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $A \\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Given that $\\mathbf x = \\langle x,y,z\\rangle$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535101 false] [17592186091972 1100 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-2x+5y-2z=-2 \\\\ -3y+z=-2 \\\\ 3x-7y+3z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $A \\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}.$ Given that $\\mathbf x = \\langle x,y,z\\rangle$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053808/assets/add80202102548e61880979bc0379e0bc65f9ef7fa37173f9035410661e2b75e.png)" 13194139535101 true] [17592186091973 1145 "First, we organize the system so that the variables are in the correct order and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+3y+z=0 \\\\ 0x+4y+z=7 \\\\ 2x-y+0z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $\\mathbf{x}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053808/assets/97d3c148b792d9db50bc81b8c12f1574f284746cb37b12d99a8881853bf5ea13.png)\n\nNow, the solution to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is given by $\\mathbf{x}= A^{-1}\\mathbf{b}.$ So, we compute $A^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1*: Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1)-3(-2)+(-8) \\\\  & =1+6-8 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2*: Compute the matrix of minors.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -7 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3*:  Find the matrix of cofactors.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053808/assets/e93ae11a2b2d1538c4ad97bba6d92e8e17fe14c8778898365ffeda9c5d1bacee.png)\n\n*Step 4*: Transpose the matrix of cofactors.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053808/assets/c2492650916d7a880ea52322edb41b8127b4c31bcff0620cec3cf4e37fa7928f.png)\n\n*Step 5*: Apply the inverse matrix formula.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14053808/assets/dd70742ae3c6613f78305edc718b10568269b49be611643059a1e6121828f404.png)\n\nFinally, we can calculate the solution as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -33\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=3,$ $y=10,$ $z=-33.$" 13194139535101 true] [17592186091973 1145 "First, we organize the system so that the variables are in the correct order and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+3y+z=0 \\\\ 0x+4y+z=7 \\\\ 2x-y+0z=-4\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $\\mathbf{x}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{b}$ is given by $\\mathbf{x}= A^{-1}\\mathbf{b}.$ So, we compute $A^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1*: Find the determinant of $A.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1)-3(-2)+(-8) \\\\  & =1+6-8 \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2*: Compute the matrix of minors.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -8 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -7 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3*:  Find the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -8 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n*Step 4*: Transpose the matrix of cofactors.\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -8 & 7 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n*Step 5*: Apply the inverse matrix formula.\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -8 & 7 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFinally, we can calculate the solution as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 10 \\\\ -33\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=3,$ $y=10,$ $z=-33.$" 13194139535101 false] [17592186092132 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331143 13194139535101 true] [17592186092132 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331150 13194139535101 true] [17592186092132 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331157 13194139535101 true] [17592186092133 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331135 13194139535101 true] [17592186092134 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331164 13194139535101 true] [17592186092134 1020 #edb/ref 17592186331171 13194139535101 true] [17592186284860 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331142 13194139535101 true] [17592186331135 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331136 13194139535101 true] [17592186331135 1089 "q-10076" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331135 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535101 true] [17592186331135 1100 "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y+3z=0 \\\\ 8x-3y+5z=9 \\\\ 7x-2y+4z=-1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331135 1113 #uuid "1f56f052-82ef-5f6f-b9cb-411952681c67" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331135 1145 "We wish to write this system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(-12+10)+2(32-35)+3(-16+21) \\\\  & =-8-6+15 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}8 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}8 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 4\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 5\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 8 & -3\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -5 & 6 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{1}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}19 \\\\ -49 \\\\ -58\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence the solution is $x=19,y=-49,z=-58.$" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331137 13194139535101 true] [17592186331136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331138 13194139535101 true] [17592186331136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331139 13194139535101 true] [17592186331136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331140 13194139535101 true] [17592186331136 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331141 13194139535101 true] [17592186331136 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535101 true] [17592186331136 1041 "selection" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331136 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331141 13194139535101 true] [17592186331136 1110 #uuid "b1033273-5d4f-5a9d-b005-946c4dd7384e" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331137 1034 "x=42,y=-35,z=9" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331137 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535101 true] [17592186331137 1111 #uuid "455280a6-f859-5054-803b-696ef3129529" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331138 1034 "x=-19,y=-49,z=-58" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331138 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535101 true] [17592186331138 1111 #uuid "d84f689a-134f-5407-b5f7-e046f6e72b21" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331139 1034 "x=15,y=-49,z=-58" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331139 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535101 true] [17592186331139 1111 #uuid "ee0c1bfc-c0b0-5476-9eff-a10057ad340a" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331140 1034 "x=19,y=49,z=58" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331140 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535101 true] [17592186331140 1111 #uuid "49684f5f-864b-59c5-b876-5b3a8697f322" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331141 1034 "x=19,y=-49,z=-58" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331141 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535101 true] [17592186331141 1111 #uuid "ac85153a-3e2f-5e94-8d8d-4602905ebb9c" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331142 1034 "1" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331142 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535101 true] [17592186331142 1111 #uuid "2cf19437-06f3-5ea2-9f83-78e1cabbc712" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331143 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331144 13194139535101 true] [17592186331143 1089 "q-78421" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331143 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535101 true] [17592186331143 1100 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x-2y+3z=0 \\\\ 8x-3y+5z=1 \\\\ 7x-2y+4z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331143 1113 #uuid "db6060ad-8c77-548e-9bad-ddb7a1172d78" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331143 1145 "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -6 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=1,y=-1,z=-2.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=1+(-1)+(-2)=-2.$" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331144 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331145 13194139535101 true] [17592186331144 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331146 13194139535101 true] [17592186331144 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331147 13194139535101 true] [17592186331144 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331148 13194139535101 true] [17592186331144 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331149 13194139535101 true] [17592186331144 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535101 true] [17592186331144 1041 "selection" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331144 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331149 13194139535101 true] [17592186331144 1110 #uuid "d49f56c9-7e65-583a-b934-0a287de9762e" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331145 1034 "3" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331145 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535101 true] [17592186331145 1111 #uuid "29842345-b6c2-5d6d-9d82-89a73f9b97e5" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331146 1034 "-3" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331146 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535101 true] [17592186331146 1111 #uuid "356ed408-1e33-568a-bd26-e3307d2b9b8b" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331147 1034 "0" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331147 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535101 true] [17592186331147 1111 #uuid "c74ce52f-ebd5-5b5a-8ff2-96579f6a2943" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331148 1034 "-1" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331148 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535101 true] [17592186331148 1111 #uuid "73afc0ce-73e9-5fc7-8fbe-f9ac34f81ae8" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331149 1034 "-2" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331149 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535101 true] [17592186331149 1111 #uuid "864583e4-523f-5dfa-880c-aec63263656e" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331150 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331151 13194139535101 true] [17592186331150 1089 "q-78551" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331150 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535101 true] [17592186331150 1100 "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-y+z=1 \\\\ 3x+2y-z=1 \\\\ x-4y+3z=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=⟨x,y,z⟩$ is unique, what is the value of $x+y+z?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -10 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -14 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331150 1113 #uuid "6b5a6d2e-84ca-5b1b-8229-e89b616a1853" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331150 1145 "First, let's write our system in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ax & =b \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -10 & 2 & 4 \\\\ -14 & 3 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution is $x=1,y=-2,z=-2.$\n\nFinally, $x+y+z=1+(-2)+(-2)=-3.$" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331151 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331152 13194139535101 true] [17592186331151 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331153 13194139535101 true] [17592186331151 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331154 13194139535101 true] [17592186331151 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331155 13194139535101 true] [17592186331151 1000 #edb/ref 17592186331156 13194139535101 true] [17592186331151 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535101 true] [17592186331151 1041 "selection" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331151 1104 #edb/ref 17592186331154 13194139535101 true] [17592186331151 1110 #uuid "6036be45-3f7b-5236-9670-640a998a7124" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331152 1034 "7" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331152 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535101 true] [17592186331152 1111 #uuid "9535c375-2d54-5e41-a8f0-e3d677a695ff" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331153 1034 "2" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331153 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535101 true] [17592186331153 1111 #uuid "78413cf9-4770-5672-a06b-5c736541e297" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331154 1034 "-3" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331154 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535101 true] [17592186331154 1111 #uuid "125c1985-9152-5da8-abc1-0fa65030f129" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331155 1034 "-1" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331155 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535101 true] [17592186331155 1111 #uuid "442dac3f-64fb-54c6-b5d4-53c435ee3c63" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331156 1034 "-2" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331156 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535101 true] [17592186331156 1111 #uuid "cea4aaeb-7ba5-5cc5-b409-5efa13136c72" 13194139535101 true] [17592186331157 1017 #edb/ref 17592186331158 1319413